A bind gives the thread spare time whatever the invoked capability's rights.
A thread lent units without RIGHT_X to hold it to them would run on spare time all the same;
a binding carries no more rights than the capability it was made through.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: slot is not derived from its parent
Witness: fuzz lend-lender-earns

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -766,7 +766,7 @@ static int op_time(struct thread *t, uint32_t slot, const struct cap *cap,
             return KERR_LIMIT;
         }
         /* The binding hangs below the invoked capability, so a revoke above it empties the place. */
-        sched_bind(p, first, count, cap->rights, slot_node(t, slot), span);
+        sched_bind(p, first, count, RIGHT_W | RIGHT_X, slot_node(t, slot), span);
         return KERR_OK;
     }
     default:
